        <mxCell id="c56" value="&lt;i&gt;A sketch of Tutorial 15.2, Step 9, all cost centers together. The vertical axis starts at 6.0M, not at zero, so that the small steps show; the two blue bars are cut near the base. The classification effect moves 101,828.64 up in Warehouse and down in Administration, so it explains none of the total; what remains, 174,758.97 below the budget, is a few percent nearly everywhere.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="538" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
